   287	unanswered.
   288	
   289	## 6. Objectives, references, and checks
   290	
   291	### 6.1 Profit
   292	
   293	Focal per-seed normalised gain g = (pi - pi_ref) / (S*/N), with S* the seed's first-best surplus; the cell's estimate is
   294	the mean over seeds.
   295	
   296	### 6.2 Welfare (sabotage), headline only
   297	
   298	- W0: minimise expected gross efficiency, no constraint.
   299	- W1: the rule's final reference (6.4) is frozen first; then minimise expected gross efficiency subject to
   300	  E[(pi_focal - pi_ref) / (S*/N)] >= 0 on the dev-train seeds. Selection is feasibility-first: among evaluated points that
   301	  satisfy the constraint on the training seeds, the lowest training efficiency; if none, the report says "no feasible
   302	  candidate found" (a bounded search cannot prove infeasibility). On the evaluation seeds the constraint mean is
   303	  re-estimated with its nominal 95 percent interval and classified: lower bound >= 0, profitability supported; upper
   304	  bound < 0, profitability contradicted; otherwise unresolved. A W1 attack is called profitable only when supported.
   305	- Both on the D2+H3 and X7-SC knob spaces; winners selected on training seeds. Reported per rule and objective: the
   306	  training-selected winner (the lower training efficiency of the two families) evaluated unchanged on the evaluation
   307	  seeds, its interval, and the attacker's gain; the other family's result is reported beside it. No extremum is selected
   308	  on evaluation data.
   309	
   310	### 6.3 Coalition, headline only
   311	
   312	Members are `sim/policies/exploratory.py::coalition_members(cfg, focal, c)`: the focal provider, then the providers
   313	nearest to it in the positions score order, ties to the lower index; member j of that ordered list (j = 0 is the focal
   314	provider) gets schedule index j. Members play shared knobs with member schedules (X6-SE/v2) or the decoy and beneficiary
   315	roles (X8-DB, c = 2); non-members play honest-max. Member gain
   316	g_j = (pi_j - pi_j^0) / (S*/N), where pi_j^0 is member j's profit under the frozen joint truthful reference of that
   317	coalition (one per rule, market, and c). Objectives: total G_tot = sum_j E[g_j] and worst member G_min = min_j E[g_j]
   318	(not E[min_j g_j]).
   319	
   320	Because G_tot's reference term is a constant, the G_tot searches do not need the reference; G_min's do. Truthful
   321	projection of a coalition profile (spec 5.2, `Family.project`): every member's claim is clipped to its effort
   322	(clip = 1 for X6-SE/v2 members; for X8-DB the beneficiary's clip = 1 and every decoy knob, including u_D, n_D, and w_D,
   323	unchanged, since the decoy's claim already equals its effort). Order per rule and c, all on dev-train seeds:
   324	
   325	1. The joint twins: the registered search (5 restarts x 300) over the X6-SE/v2 knobs with clip = 1 forced for every
   326	   member, maximising sum_j (pi_j / (S*/N)), once with the synchronised and once with the staggered schedule.
   327	2. The G_tot searches (X6-SE/v2 synchronised and staggered; X8-DB at c = 2).
   328	3. Preliminary reference: the candidate with the highest training mean of sum_j (pi_j / (S*/N)) among, in this tie
   329	   order: all members honest-max, all members abstain, the synchronised twin, the staggered twin, then the truthful
   330	   projections of the step-2 winners and of every point in their archives, in search order.
   331	4. The G_min searches against the preliminary reference, with the reference profile inserted as an incumbent where the
   332	   family can represent it.
   333	5. Final reference: the same rule over the step-3 menu plus the truthful projections of the step-4 winners and archive
   334	   points, in search order; freeze.
   335	6. Every archived G_min point (step 4) is rescored against the final reference on the same training seeds; the final
   336	   reference profile itself is added as a candidate wherever the G_min family can represent it (it scores exactly zero
   337	   against itself); the G_min winner is the best of these candidates. G_tot winners are unchanged (constant reference
   338	   term). Then evaluation. Required regression test: a final reference taken from a step-5 projection, with every
   339	   archived point negative against it, selects the reference profile where it is representable.
   340	
   341	Claims are gains relative to this coordinated truthful profile; they say nothing about coalition stability or each
   342	member's best unilateral alternative.
   343	
   344	### 6.4 References and freeze order
   345	
   346	- **Menu.** A rule's truthful reference is selected on training seeds by the registered order (spec 5.2) from one menu:
   347	  abstain, honest-max, and the twin, projection, and archive candidates of its D2+H3 and X7-SC searches. Every rule in the
   348	  evaluation, including B2 and the rho = 1 repair cells, has exactly these two searches at the same budget (8.1), so
   349	  matched pairs have equivalent menus. **Exception:** the secondary whole systems (B3-t, R3-t, C*-t) on fresh markets
   350	  have no X7-SC cell (8.1); their fresh-market reference menu is abstain, honest-max, and the D2+H3 candidates, the same
   351	  reduced menu for all three systems, and their fresh-market results are labelled accordingly. Its D2, X5-AG/v2, H4, and welfare gains use the same frozen reference; no other
   352	  family adds candidates. Coalitions use their own joint reference (6.3).
   353	- **Development reference** (tuning, comparator selection): the same construction with the tuning objective's families
   354	  (D2, D2+H3, X7-SC) on the tuning markets. H4 is never available in development.
   355	- **Dependency and freeze order per market.** (1) Profit attack and twin searches and banks; (2) reference selection and
   356	  freeze; (3) the searches that need a frozen reference (W1) and the coalition steps 1 to 6 of 6.3 in their order; (4) envelope
   357	  family choices (9.3 Q3), the fixed-attack bank and its training-seed matrix (6.6); (5) final freeze. Only then may any
   358	  evaluation-seed episode of that market run; the evaluation stage refuses to run otherwise. Doubling results never enter
   359	  the frozen candidates (6.5 says how they are used).
   360	
   361	### 6.5 Search-quality checks
   362	
   363	A doubling check continues the registered search with as many additional restarts as the registered budget (new restart
   364	seeds), so the total budget doubles; it is reported as a diagnostic. Scheduled checks (fixed in the manifest):
   365	
   366	- headline: the 10 matched rules (F000 to F111, C*, C*/S0) x {D2+H3, X7-SC} (20), the 12 welfare cells, and the 30
   367	  coalition cells (24 X6-SE/v2, 6 X8-DB);
   368	- fresh markets: the Q1 and Q4 rules (F000, F111, C*) x {D2+H3, X7-SC} x 6 (36).
   369	
   370	98 checks. Units and threshold 0.005: gain (normalised by S*/N) for profit; G_tot and G_min (each normalised) for
   371	coalitions; gross efficiency (a share of the first best) for welfare. Attack-profit and reference-profit changes are
   372	reported separately. A W1 check that finds a feasible point where the original found none, or a feasible point with
   373	efficiency lower by at least 0.005, labels the cell incomplete. Cells without a scheduled check (factorial cells on fresh
   374	markets, whole systems, X5, H4, D2 extras) carry no search-quality claim.
   375	
   376	**Two statuses.** A cell is **missing** if it did not run to completion or is invalid: not run (cap stop or cut), a
   377	refused sample, a nonfinite statistic (9.2), a search with no finite candidate, or a failed load (H4). A cell is
   378	**search-flagged** if it ran to completion but its scheduled doubling check exceeded the threshold above ("incomplete" in
   379	the check's own wording). Consequences: a missing cell removes every confirmatory decision that uses it (the test is
   380	reported "not decided: missing cell") and makes that part of its question unanswered (8.1a). A search-flagged cell keeps
   381	its estimate as the estimate of the prescribed (frozen) search procedure; a confirmatory decision that uses it is still
   382	made and is reported as a decision about the prescribed search procedure only; the robustness statement for that rule
   383	and family (Q3) is reported unanswered ("search flagged"), never as "no attack found". **Held-out diagnostic:** for every scheduled check, the doubled search's winner (selected on its training
   384	seeds) is evaluated unchanged on the cell's evaluation seeds against the same frozen reference, and reported beside the
   385	cell; it never replaces or adds to the frozen estimate.
   386	
   387	### 6.6 Fixed-attack cross-evaluation (Q2)
   388	
   389	For each market and family in {D2+H3, X7-SC}: the bank is the 8 selected attacks of the 8 factorial cells (frozen with
   390	the references). Each attack is evaluated against all 8 factorial rules on the evaluation seeds, each against its own
   391	frozen reference: an 8 x 8 gain matrix. For every fixed-attack contrast the report gives the gain contrast and its two
   392	terms separately, since g_R(a) - g_C(a) = [pi_R(a) - pi_C(a)] / (S*/N) - [pi_R(r_R) - pi_C(r_C)] / (S*/N): the change in
   393	attacker profit and the change in the truthful reference payoff; beside them, gross and net efficiency. Fixed-attack
   394	contrasts use the same effect coding as 9.3 within each attack's row, then the equal-weight mean over the 8 rows (an
   395	average over this bank, not over attacks in general). **Bank envelope:** the same 8 x 8 matrix is also evaluated on the
   396	dev-train seeds of the registered search (part of step 4 of the freeze order); for each rule the attack with the highest
   397	training gain is selected there and its evaluation-seed gain is reported with its nominal interval. No extremum is
   398	selected on evaluation data.
   399	
   400	### 6.7 Honest-replacement diagnostic (descriptive)
   401	
   402	Whether inspection of a replacement ends: on the headline market, the focal provider plays honest-max, replaces its
   403	identity once at round 50, and plays honest-max after; every other provider plays honest-max. Rules F000, F111, and C*;
   404	the 200 evaluation seeds; no search. Reported per identity age (rounds since the replacement's creation, in bins of 10):
   405	the share of the focal provider's served jobs that are audited, its profit per round, and its refunds from false
   406	failures. Three fixed-policy cells; the cost is evaluation episodes only.
   407	
   408	## 7. Market instances and randomness
   409	
   410	### 7.1 Generator (a synthetic neighbourhood of the headline market)
   411	
   412	`instance(stream) -> MarketConfig` with fixed N = 10, J = 50, T = 200, sigma = 0.05, eta = 0, beta = 0.05, rho = 0.2,
   413	v_min = 0.6, and per draw: q_max = 10 sorted draws from Uniform[0.55, 1.0]; b_lo ~ U[0.18, 0.26], b_hi ~ U[0.34, 0.46],
   414	b_i = b_hi - (b_hi - b_lo) * rank_i / 9 + U[-0.02, 0.02] (rank by q_max, ascending; the negative quality-cost association
   415	of the headline market); a_i ~ U[0, 0.05]; k_i uniform in {4, ..., 8}; v_max ~ U[1.2, 1.6]. Draws repeat inside the same
   416	stream until `MarketConfig.validate()` passes (at most 10,000; the count is recorded). Calibration per instance with the
   417	frozen calibrate on seeds 4000 to 4019. The claim population is this neighbourhood: fixed scale, noise, budget ratio,
   418	audit cost, and cost-quality association.
   419	
   420	### 7.2 Streams
   421	
   422	- Digest: d(root, domain, n) = SHA-256 of the ASCII bytes of root + "|touchstone-v2|" + domain + "|" + decimal(n).
   423	- Instance stream i: `numpy.random.Generator(numpy.random.PCG64(int.from_bytes(d(root, "instance", i)[:16], "big")))`.
   424	- Development root: the string "dev-20261022"; `dev0`, `dev1` = instance streams 0 and 1. Public now.
   425	- Fresh root: the block hash at height H (7.3) as 64 lowercase hex characters in the usual big-endian display order;
   426	  fresh instances = streams 0 to 5, labelled `fresh0` to `fresh5`. If a stream hits the 10,000-draw limit, it is replaced
   427	  by the next stream index (6, 7, ...), in order, keeping the labels in order.
   428	- Evaluation seeds for market label m in {`headline`, `fresh0`, ..., `fresh5`}: v_n = 30,000,000 +
   429	  int.from_bytes(d(root, "seeds/" + m, n)[:8], "big") mod 10,000,000 for n = 0, 1, ...; duplicates skipped; the first 200.
   430	  The range [30,000,000, 40,000,000) is disjoint from every reserved range (`sim/amendment.py`, the amendment-1 block
   431	  ending at 9,000,000, the final-evaluation range) and from the new coverage range (9.5), checked by a test.
   432	- Identity salt: d(root, "salt", 0) in hex. It is public after the draw; rules never receive the salt or entity ids
   433	  (spec 4.0), which a test enforces.
   434	
   435	### 7.3 Block height and finality
   436	
   437	- **Anchor.** The protocol file is stamped with OpenTimestamps and the proof is upgraded until it holds a Bitcoin
   438	  attestation. A = the lowest Bitcoin block height attested in the upgraded proof, as reported by `ots verify`. H = A + 144.
   439	  The rule, not the number, is in the protocol file; H follows deterministically.
   440	- **Publication.** One authoritative protocol: the signed tag, the protocol file, and the upgraded proof are pushed to
   441	  the public repository before block H is mined. If that deadline fails, the original draw is kept and reported, but its
   442	  results are labelled nonconfirmatory; any replacement registration must be public before its own target block.
   443	- **Reading.** The hash at H is read once both explorers (blockstream.info and mempool.space) report a tip height of at
   444	  least H + 6 and give the same hash at H. If they disagree, the reader waits one hour and reads again, until they agree at
   445	  a tip of at least H + 6; the first agreeing read is final. The reader also downloads the headers from A to H + 6 and
   446	  checks every hash link and proof of work from A's header, whose Merkle root carries the protocol commitment. Trust
   447	  assumption stated in the paper: the chain both explorers serve at the final read is the accepted chain; a later
   448	  reorganisation deeper than 6 blocks is not handled, and would be reported. A second assumption: no miner chooses the
   449	  block at H to influence this evaluation.
   450	- **Confirmation draw.** If a substantive fix is needed after outcomes (9.6), the fixed code and an amendment are locked
   451	  and stamped the same way, giving anchor A2; the fixed code is evaluated on fresh markets and seeds from the block at
   452	  H2 = A2 + 144, and both results are reported.
   453	
   454	## 8. Manifest and compute
   455	
   456	### 8.1 Cells (focal provider at the median position; markets: headline + 6 fresh = 7)
   457	
   458	| Block | Rules | Families | Markets | Cells |
   459	|---|---|---|---|---|
   460	| Matched factorial and comparator | F000..F111, C*, C*/S0 (10) | D2+H3, X7-SC | 7 | 140 |
   461	| Matched core extras | F000, F111, C* | D2, X5-AG/v2, H4 | 7 | 63 |
   462	| Whole systems | B3-t, R3-t, C*-t | D2+H3 (7 markets), X7-SC (headline) | 7 / 1 | 24 |
   463	| Reference | B2 | D2, D2+H3, X7-SC | headline | 3 |
   464	| Welfare | F000, F111, C* | W0, W1 x {D2+H3, X7-SC} | headline | 12 |
   465	| Coalition | F000, F111, C* | X6-SE/v2: c {2, 5} x {sync, staggered} x {total, min}; X8-DB: c = 2 x {total, min} | headline | 30 |
   466	| Repair test | F000, F111, R4, C*, C*/S2 | D2, D2+H3, X7-SC | headline at rho = 1 | 15 |
   467	| Diagnostic (6.7) | F000, F111, C* | honest replacement, fixed | headline | 3 (no search) |
   468	
   469	287 search cells (85 on the X7-SC knob space, 21 H4 cells priced as X7-SC), 3 fixed-policy cells, 14 fixed-attack
   470	cross-evaluations (6.6), 98 doubling checks (6.5). Every cell is evaluated on 200 seeds. Draft 6's R4 and C*/S2 cells at
   471	rho = 0.2 (61 cells) duplicated R3 and C* (3.4) and are removed; the whole-system X7-SC cells on fresh markets and R4-t
   472	are removed to fund X8-DB and the diagnostics.
   473	
   474	### 8.1a Questions and their cells
   475	
   476	Statuses as in 6.5: a missing required cell makes that part unanswered (and removes the confirmatory decisions that use
   477	it); a search-flagged cell keeps confirmatory decisions (labelled as about the prescribed search procedure) and makes the
   478	Q3 robustness statement for that rule and family unanswered. Scheduled doubling checks (6.5) are listed with their
   479	question.
   480	
   481	| Question | Required cells, and scheduled checks |
   482	|---|---|
   483	| Q1 (confirmatory) | F111 and C* x {D2+H3, X7-SC} x 6 fresh markets, with their references; checks: those 24 cells; descriptive: headline, C*/S0 |
   484	| Q2 (descriptive) | the 8 factorial cells x {D2+H3, X7-SC} x 7 markets and the 14 cross-evaluations; checks: the headline factorial cells (16) |
   485	| Q3 (descriptive) | per core rule (F000, F111, C*): D2+H3, X7-SC, X5-AG/v2, H4 on 7 markets; welfare; coalitions; the diagnostic. If H4 is cut on fresh markets (8.2) or fails to load, the independently authored part of Q3 is reported as not run on those markets, never as "no attack found"; checks: every core-rule profit, welfare, and coalition check of 6.5 |
   486	| Q4 (confirmatory) | F000 and F111 x D2+H3 x 6 fresh markets, with their references; checks: those 12 cells |
   487	| Repair | the rho = 1 block |
   488	| Whole systems (secondary) | B3-t, R3-t, C*-t cells |
   489	
   490	### 8.2 Cost
   491	
   492	Unit: one headline D2+H3 cell (search, bank, reference, 40-seed evaluation) at the registered budget, about 25
